      "ruled": "2026-07-30",
      "why": "NOT held out — EXCLUDED BY RECORD SHAPE, and the distinction matters. The human ruling is a DECLINE: \"Playing Meowth during setup doesnt allow us to use Last-Ditch Catch ability, thus should be avoided when able.\" A decline needs `correct: []`, which `decision` scope forbids (`build_correction` requires `correct` non-empty and indexing a legal option; all 10 corpus records carrying `correct: []` are `turn` scope). With ONE option and `minCount 0` the record degenerates to `chosen == correct == [0]`, so grading a decider against it scores the CORRECT decline as a REGRESSION.\n\nThe sweep now skips this shape on its own terms (`_records_a_decline_it_cannot_state`: an OPTIONAL select asserting the agent's own pick), so NO Held-out Ledger entry exists and no owner is invented for what is a schema limit rather than another issue's work. Deliberately narrow — a MANDATORY select with `chosen == correct` states a real preference and still gates.\n\nThe behaviour is gated by `tests/strategy/test_setup_bench_decline.py::test_f3_declines_pre_benching_the_supporter_tutor`, which asserts the decline on this board.\n\nHistory: ADR-0084 Amendment F briefly overturned this on 2026-07-30 (with no other Pokémon in hand, declining leaves a one-body board) and was WITHDRAWN the same day on the user's narrowing — `docs/rules.md` §2 puts my first turn before the first legal attack in either seat, so the tutor can be benched on turn 1 and still fire Last-Ditch Catch. Waiting costs nothing; benching costs the Ability. Bench on an empty Bench only when the Active is doomed or a specific Supporter is needed — neither holds at a pregame placement, where the Ability cannot fire at all."
    }
